      "id": "CoreDesign.Data",
      "range": "[1.1.0, )"
    },
    "message": "CoreDesign.Data ships a full audit layer: AuditInterceptor sets audit fields automatically on every save via ICurrentUserAccessor, so user IDs no longer need to be passed to repository methods. Delete operations are now explicit — SoftDeleteAsync, HardDeleteAsync, and cascade variants walk the EF navigation graph for child entities. MigrationWorker gains PurgeBeforeSeed to replace seed content on deploy, and CoreDesignSeedFactory<TContext> is the integration point for the new CoreDesign.SeedTool dotnet tool. See the release notes and documentation for details.",
    "reasons": [
      "Legacy"
    ]
  },
  "description": "A generic, reusable Entity Framework Core data access layer providing base entity infrastructure and repository abstractions for .NET projects.",
